{"claims": [
  {
    "text": "The driver's arrival is established on the trace itself: the derived arrival block places the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 06:54:40, records 25 qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius for this zone class, and the closest approach recorded anywhere in the trace is 5.4 m from the pickup pin. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) are satisfied on the driver's own COMPLETE, weight-1.0 device telemetry - this is not a driver who never reached the pickup.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00408", "EV-TRIP-00408"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
    "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.fix_count",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The termination side of the record favours the driver's account: the trip is recorded CANCELLED_BY_DRIVER at 06:58:40 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, which is one of the three codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises, and there is no boarding event anywhere on the record (started_at and ended_at are null). The reason-code and no-boarding elements of limb (d) are therefore met, and the only element of this episode the driver loses on is the length of his dwell.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00408", "EV-GPS-00408"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The arrival marker is true and not false: the arrived event at 06:54:40 is also the first qualifying in-geofence fix, so the marker was not pressed from more than 300 m out and not at 15 km/h or more. POL-NS-05 is not engaged on this trip and no false-arrival event should be recorded against this driver in the ruling's referrals.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00408", "EV-TRIP-00408"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-02"],
    "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The rider's own telemetry contradicts his account that he came down and the car was gone: his 27 fixes run from 06:54:40 to 06:58:34 at a flat 0.0 km/h and lie between 496.9 m and 503.8 m from the pickup pin, so his qualifying-fix count inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius is 0. POL-NS-04 limb (c) is therefore affirmatively failed on admissible fixes, the clause cannot exonerate the rider, and the dispute returns to POL-NS-01.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00408", "EV-TRIP-00408"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-01"],
    "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The rider never once wrote to the driver during the waiting window: the chat log carries two entries only - the system's 'Your driver has arrived' at 06:54:41 and the driver's own 'here at blk 621' at 06:55:00 - so POL-NS-04 limb (a) fails as well, and the rider's complaint that he was let down is unsupported by his own conduct. Disclosure: EV-CHAT-00408 is IMPAIRED at weight 0.85 on issue code UNREAD_MESSAGE (both messages delivered, read_at null); that impairment bears only on whether the messages were read, not on whether the rider sent any, so the point survives the discount.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00408", "EV-TRIP-00408"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-GEN-02"],
    "asserted_weight": 0.85
  },
  {
    "text": "Concession on the one element the record does not give the driver: the derived arrival block measures his continuous in-geofence dwell at 240 seconds (25 fixes, 06:54:40 to 06:58:40), while this trip's platform_policy_in_force carries free_wait_sec of 300 seconds - a shortfall of 60 seconds - so under POL-NS-06 the cancellation fee is not chargeable whether or not the rider was present, and no driver compensation is payable. I do not contest that arithmetic and I do not ask the Judge to read the period in force as anything other than the 300 seconds this record carries. What the record equally does not support is any finding that the driver was absent or that the rider was at the pin; the driver's difficulty is the clock, not the facts.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00408", "EV-TRIP-00408"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-07"],
    "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "If the Judge does find the dwell element satisfied, the emitted ruling must be DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd SGD 3.20 and not NO_ACTION: POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee in force - SGD 3.20, which is the figure the fare breakdown's own driver_compensation field carries - and POL-GEN-03 requires the ruling value to name the outcome the case produces, with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd on that one ruling.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00408", "EV-TRIP-00408"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-03"],
    "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "Nothing on either profile supports withholding the driver's money or escalating this case: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against completed_trips_30d of 120, so the count is not 4 or more and the rate is 0.0083, well under 0.08, and POL-NS-07's anti-farming branch is not tripped; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0, so no POL-NS-09(c) or (d) trigger exists. The lifetime prior_no_show_flags counters are not the trailing-window fields these clauses read and may not be substituted for them.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00408", "EV-RPROF-00408"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-01"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The bundle is clean on the facts that decide this case: the fare line reconciles with the figure in force (cancellation_fee SGD 4.00 equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged), the trace carries 50 fixes at a uniform 10-second cadence with zero gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0, and the arrived event matches the first in-geofence fix to the second, so there is no clock skew under POL-NS-08(a) and no trace defect under limb (b). The chat log holds exactly the two messages the trip record counts, so limb (c) is not engaged either: the UNREAD_MESSAGE tag on EV-CHAT-00408 (weight 0.85) satisfies none of POL-NS-08's limbs and down-weights confidence under POL-GEN-02 only. The deciding facts rest on weight-1.0 telemetry, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is not engaged by anything relied on here.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00408", "EV-GPS-00408", "EV-TRIP-00408", "EV-CHAT-00408"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-GEN-02"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  }
]}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Summary: the driver's arrival is confirmed on the record, but his wait was 60 seconds short of the free waiting period in force, so the $4.00 no-show fee was not chargeable. Because the fee has already been refunded, his request to have it reinstated is not supported and nothing further moves.\n\nARRIVAL — accepted. EV-GPS-00408 (weight 1.00) puts the first fix inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at 06:54:40, exactly the timestamp of the 'arrived' tap, and holds 25 qualifying fixes inside the radius. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) are met. Because the marker coincides with the first qualifying in-geofence fix (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0), POL-NS-05 is not engaged: the marker is not false, and no false-arrival referral is recorded against the driver on that ground.\n\nDWELL — decisive, and both sides agree on the arithmetic. EV-TRIP-00408 (weight 1.00) carries a free waiting period of 300 seconds (platform_policy.free_wait_sec); EV-GPS-00408 measures a single continuous in-geofence stay of 240 seconds, from 06:54:40 to the cancellation at 06:58:40 — a 60-second shortfall. POL-NS-01(c) requires the full 300 seconds measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the tap, and limb (d) requires termination at or after that dwell elapsed; both fail. POL-NS-06 therefore applies: the fee is not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full, whether or not she was present or replied. No accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) is possible — the trace shows run_count 1 with no second interval, and the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00408-01 is MISSING at weight 0.00, so limb (i) is unavailable rather than exculpatory.\n\nDRIVER'S CLAIMS. His arrival claims (POL-NS-01(a)–(b), POL-NS-05) are accepted. His concession that the dwell was 240 seconds against 300 is accepted and is decisive. His conditional claim that a satisfied dwell would yield DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.20 (80% of the SGD 4.00 fee, the figure in the money block) is not reached: POL-NS-06 displaces POL-NS-01, so no compensation issues. His claims that the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1, below the required 4, against 120 completed trips in 30 days, a rate of 0.008 against the 0.08 threshold) and that no POL-NS-09 trigger fires are accepted; the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counters are context only under POL-GEN-01 and were not used as a ground.\n\nRIDER'S CLAIMS. Her account that the driver did not wait five minutes is corroborated by the timestamps and accepted; her claims that the fee is not chargeable, that no payout is owed, and that the disposition is NO_ACTION are accepted. Her own telemetry (27 fixes, 0.0 km/h, 496.9–503.8 m from the pin, 0 qualifying fixes inside the 100 m rider-presence radius) means POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate her — but that changes nothing, because POL-NS-06 refunds the fee regardless of rider presence.\n\nESCALATION AND REFERRALS — none. Confidence is above the 0.70 floor; the trace is unimpaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d) (zero gaps, uniform 10-second cadence, arrival event matching the first fix to the second, and the SGD 4.00 fare line reconciling with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd); both counterparty-dispute counters are 0; the anti-farming check is not tripped. The rider's account that she came down is contradicted by her own track, but that is a statement against one unimpaired artifact, not two admissible artifacts in direct conflict under POL-NS-09(b), and in any event POL-NS-06 decides the fee whether or not she was present. No clause produces a referral, so the list is empty.\n\nEVIDENCE WEIGHTS. The deciding facts rest on EV-GPS-00408 and EV-TRIP-00408, both weight 1.00 and both unimpaired under POL-NS-08, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.00 and confidence is 0.95. EV-CHAT-00408 is impaired at weight 0.85 for UNREAD_MESSAGE (both entries delivered, no read receipt); it carries no deciding fact and only discounts confidence under POL-GEN-02.\n\nDISPOSITION. NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03. The driver filed to have the charge reinstated; that claim is not supported by the evidence, the present state stands, and the $4.00 already refunded (refund_issued_sgd 4.00, payment_status REFUNDED) stays refunded. No refund and no compensation is ordered: amount_sgd null, driver_compensation_sgd null. The monetary effect is SGD 0.00, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so nothing is held for release. This ruling was made without human review; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04 within 30 days."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The 240 seconds cannot be padded into 300 on any reading. POL-NS-06(i) permits separate in-geofence intervals to be summed only where a present and populated traffic advisory of type KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT covers the pickup road and window, and there is no second interval to sum in any event — the trace shows a single in-geofence run with no excursion. The advisory artifact is MISSING, and the policy says a MISSING traffic_advisory makes limb (i) unavailable rather than exonerating anyone; its absence is itself citable.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00408-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
